Description: stock quotes in the GNOME top bar
 Stockbar shows a watchlist of stocks, indices, currencies and crypto in the
 GNOME Shell top bar, with the whole list and the last update in a dropdown.
 .
 The stockbar command manages the watchlist, either in an interactive editor
 or with subcommands such as "stockbar add AAPL". A per-user background
 service fetches the quotes from CNBC, which needs no account or API key.
 .
 The first change to the watchlist turns the extension and the service on;
 log out and back in once after that.
